<title>UK: BGB Finance adds 750 mln FFR to 2009 bond.</title>
<headline>BGB Finance adds 750 mln FFR to 2009 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to 2.25 billion French francs from 1.5 billion francs, joints lead managers Caisse des Depots et Consignations and J.P. Morgan said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BGB FINANCE</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  BANKGESELLSCHAFT BERLIN GROUP</p>
<p> AMT ** 2.25 BLN FFR  COUPON     5.75	MATURITY    20.MAR.09</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  97.207    PAY DATE    28.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    95.557    SPREAD	+36 BP</p>
<p> NOTES  **  ORIGINAL 1.5 BLN FFR BOND LAUNCHED ON 24.FEB.97</p>
<p> MOODY	AA1	 LISTING    PARIS     PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> IBCA	 AAA	 DENOMS (K) 10-100-1M SALE LIMITS</p>
<p> US/UK/FE/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    35 BP     SELL CONC  1.65	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND INTERPOLATED 8.5 PCT 2008, 6.5 PCT 2011</p>
<p> OATS</p>
<p> NOTES	SUBORDINATED</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
